WEBVTT

00:00:00.075 --> 00:00:04.475
Edgepad turns an Android phone into the controls for a Windows laptop.

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:06.975
It's for when the laptop is across the room:

00:00:07.475 --> 00:00:09.575
on the TV, docked on a desk,

00:00:09.812 --> 00:00:11.362
anywhere your mouse can't reach.

00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:15.050
Remote apps usually stop at play and pause.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.325
Remote desktop wants an account and a network just to change the volume.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.387
Edgepad needs neither.

00:00:21.763 --> 00:00:23.800
You pair the phone and laptop once,

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.663
like a headset, and from then on they talk directly.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.300
On the laptop, download Edgepad dot E X E from the latest release.

00:00:33.712 --> 00:00:35.800
It's a single file with nothing to install.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.850
Windows will warn you because it isn't code-signed,

00:00:39.212 --> 00:00:41.475
so click More info, then Run anyway.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.800
Edgepad lives in the system tray,

00:00:44.188 --> 00:00:45.825
where you'll find its connection status,

00:00:46.075 --> 00:00:49.575
Macros, Start with Windows, Forget trusted phone,

00:00:49.962 --> 00:00:51.450
the log, and the docs.

00:00:52.438 --> 00:00:56.812
On the phone, install the APK and allow Nearby devices.

00:00:57.213 --> 00:01:01.213
Edgepad only uses that permission to find laptops you've already paired.

00:01:01.613 --> 00:01:03.888
Pair the two in Windows Bluetooth settings,

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:06.863
open Edgepad, and tap your laptop in the list.

00:01:07.888 --> 00:01:10.625
The first phone to connect becomes the trusted phone.

00:01:11.025 --> 00:01:14.125
After that, it reconnects every time you open the app.

00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:18.487
If the link drops, Edgepad retries ten times,

00:01:18.712 --> 00:01:21.150
two seconds apart, and tells you what it's doing.

00:01:23.062 --> 00:01:24.600
This is the control surface:

00:01:24.837 --> 00:01:26.225
four parts on one screen.

00:01:26.638 --> 00:01:28.487
The trackpad fills the middle,

00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:30.425
a dial sits in each corner,

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.800
the media panel sits between them,

00:01:33.287 --> 00:01:35.600
and a row of buttons runs across the top.

00:01:37.513 --> 00:01:38.925
One finger moves the pointer,

00:01:39.412 --> 00:01:40.450
and a tap clicks.

00:01:40.837 --> 00:01:42.850
To drag, tap, then hold and move.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:47.525
Two fingers scroll in any direction and pinch to zoom.

00:01:47.925 --> 00:01:49.913
A two-finger tap is a right click.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.050
Three and four fingers are yours to assign.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:57.312
Out of the box, three fingers left or right switch desktops,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.525
up opens Task View, down shows the desktop,

00:02:00.975 --> 00:02:02.237
and a tap opens search.

00:02:03.262 --> 00:02:06.838
Four fingers left or right cycle through open apps,

00:02:07.062 --> 00:02:09.238
like holding Alt and pressing Tab,

00:02:09.613 --> 00:02:11.162
for as long as your fingers stay down.

00:02:11.575 --> 00:02:14.075
A four-finger tap opens notifications.

00:02:15.075 --> 00:02:19.275
Under Settings, then Trackpad, you can set pointer and scroll speed,

00:02:19.562 --> 00:02:22.175
toggle natural scrolling and on-screen hints,

00:02:22.425 --> 00:02:24.200
and remap every gesture.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.725
Each corner holds a dial,

00:02:28.175 --> 00:02:31.025
drawn as a ruler that wraps around the corner of the screen.

00:02:31.425 --> 00:02:33.525
Slide along it clockwise to turn it up.

00:02:34.525 --> 00:02:36.025
A corner can control volume,

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.263
brightness, zoom, media scrubbing, the app switcher,

00:02:40.788 --> 00:02:42.713
mic level, or refresh rate.

00:02:43.113 --> 00:02:45.325
Tapping a dial triggers its own shortcut:

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.563
volume and mic mute, media plays or pauses,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.312
zoom resets, and the app switcher opens Task View.

00:02:54.312 --> 00:02:55.238
The dials are live.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.413
They show the laptop's real volume,

00:02:57.863 --> 00:03:00.650
mute state, brightness, and playback position,

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.738
and they update when you change those on the laptop itself.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.963
When you move a dial,

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.612
the laptop shows a small readout too,

00:03:08.075 --> 00:03:09.375
so you know it landed.

00:03:10.363 --> 00:03:13.650
Under Dial feel, you can tune slide sensitivity,

00:03:13.925 --> 00:03:16.188
ruler length and height, haptic ticks,

00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:17.938
and snapping to round numbers,

00:03:18.338 --> 00:03:19.588
all with a live preview.

00:03:19.975 --> 00:03:22.575
Under Corners, you choose what each corner does,

00:03:22.838 --> 00:03:23.838
or turn it off.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.363
The media panel shows the track,

00:03:27.588 --> 00:03:30.037
the app playing it, and how far in you are,

00:03:30.325 --> 00:03:33.100
with previous, play pause, and next.

00:03:33.475 --> 00:03:34.600
Every piece can move.

00:03:34.988 --> 00:03:38.037
Open Media layout, then drag and resize them.

00:03:38.438 --> 00:03:41.825
Upright and sideways layouts are saved separately.

00:03:43.738 --> 00:03:46.200
Across the top: Settings, keyboard,

00:03:46.488 --> 00:03:48.600
lock, gamepad, and macros.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.887
The lock doesn't open a screen.

00:03:51.287 --> 00:03:55.312
It changes the surface, and it has three states.

00:03:55.725 --> 00:03:57.725
Tap once to hide the dials and media,

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.463
leaving just the trackpad.

00:03:59.862 --> 00:04:00.987
Tap again to flip it:

00:04:01.412 --> 00:04:03.700
the trackpad locks and the dials come back,

00:04:04.075 --> 00:04:07.100
so the phone can sit in your pocket and still adjust the volume.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.688
Tap a third time to bring everything back.

00:04:10.112 --> 00:04:12.150
The pad always shows which mode you're in.

00:04:14.062 --> 00:04:17.413
The keyboard is a full sideways layout with function keys,

00:04:17.788 --> 00:04:20.825
numbers, arrows, Escape, and Delete.

00:04:21.213 --> 00:04:24.600
Control, Alt, and Shift can be held or tapped.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.575
Hold one while pressing another key,

00:04:27.088 --> 00:04:29.312
or tap it once to apply it to the next key.

00:04:29.713 --> 00:04:31.062
Tap it again to cancel.

00:04:31.463 --> 00:04:33.350
You can also set the key text size.

00:04:35.238 --> 00:04:37.075
Macros are created on the laptop,

00:04:37.312 --> 00:04:39.038
from Macros in the tray menu.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.413
Each one gets a name,

00:04:40.838 --> 00:04:43.225
something to launch, optional arguments,

00:04:43.375 --> 00:04:44.413
and an icon.

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:49.447
On the phone, they appear as a grid of up to fifteen buttons.

00:04:49.846 --> 00:04:52.221
The grid uses the biggest buttons that fit,

00:04:52.621 --> 00:04:56.584
so three macros show up large and fifteen show up small.

00:04:56.959 --> 00:04:58.621
Each button shows its icon,

00:04:59.084 --> 00:05:00.022
and its name if you want.

00:05:01.047 --> 00:05:02.834
The laptop sends the icons,

00:05:03.072 --> 00:05:06.221
but the phone only ever knows a macro's name and position.

00:05:06.609 --> 00:05:08.384
It never sees the command behind it.

00:05:10.284 --> 00:05:14.084
Press one finger on the trackpad and hold it still until you feel a

00:05:14.084 --> 00:05:14.484
tick.

00:05:14.884 --> 00:05:16.659
Then draw without lifting.

00:05:17.059 --> 00:05:19.547
If the stroke matches a shape you've saved in Settings,

00:05:19.909 --> 00:05:21.372
it runs whatever you bound to it:

00:05:21.859 --> 00:05:23.934
a laptop action, a macro,

00:05:24.159 --> 00:05:25.996
or hiding or locking the pad.

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:28.884
If it matches nothing, nothing happens.

00:05:30.784 --> 00:05:33.134
Under Appearance, choose dark or light,

00:05:33.397 --> 00:05:35.047
and upright or sideways.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:38.346
Under Background and pattern, set the control colour,

00:05:38.547 --> 00:05:40.459
put a solid colour, gradient,

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:42.122
or image behind the surface,

00:05:42.297 --> 00:05:43.997
and lay a grid, dots,

00:05:44.159 --> 00:05:46.209
or checker pattern over it with its own size,

00:05:46.359 --> 00:05:47.809
opacity, and colour.

00:05:48.821 --> 00:05:50.022
And if you ever get lost,

00:05:50.384 --> 00:05:52.684
the built-in guide walks you through everything.

00:05:53.084 --> 00:05:54.647
It runs on first launch,

00:05:54.909 --> 00:05:57.046
and you can reopen it anytime from Settings.

00:05:58.971 --> 00:06:00.521
The gamepad is still in development,

00:06:00.909 --> 00:06:02.134
so expect changes.

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:06.909
Right now it creates a virtual Xbox controller on the laptop through the Vi-Gem

00:06:06.909 --> 00:06:09.559
bus driver, with analog sticks and triggers.

00:06:09.959 --> 00:06:14.134
Without the driver, it falls back to keyboard keys and tells you so.

00:06:15.147 --> 00:06:16.447
Layouts come from a library:

00:06:16.846 --> 00:06:20.184
Xbox, Xbox keys, Platformer, Racing,

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:21.059
and Shooter.

00:06:21.459 --> 00:06:22.846
Every control can be added,

00:06:23.109 --> 00:06:25.772
rebound, moved, and resized.

00:06:27.684 --> 00:06:30.322
The phone and laptop talk over classic Bluetooth,

00:06:30.772 --> 00:06:32.859
on a direct R F comm link.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:37.447
No account, no Why-Fye, no server anywhere in the path.

00:06:38.459 --> 00:06:41.184
Gestures never send keyboard shortcuts.

00:06:41.584 --> 00:06:46.346
They send named actions, like "desktop right," and the laptop decides what each one

00:06:46.347 --> 00:06:46.922
means.

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:48.884
So the phone can request an action,

00:06:49.309 --> 00:06:50.634
but it can never run a command.

00:06:51.634 --> 00:06:53.322
When the link falls behind your finger,

00:06:53.572 --> 00:06:56.272
queued-up movements merge into a single update,

00:06:56.647 --> 00:06:59.609
so the pointer catches up instead of replaying the backlog.

00:07:00.622 --> 00:07:03.122
Both apps check protocol versions when they connect,

00:07:03.346 --> 00:07:05.697
so always install them from the same release.

00:07:06.697 --> 00:07:08.272
The trade-off is range.

00:07:08.684 --> 00:07:10.534
Bluetooth won't reach the next room.

00:07:12.459 --> 00:07:14.247
The phone app is written in Kotlin,

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.847
the laptop app in C sharp on dot NET.

00:07:17.259 --> 00:07:20.209
It's all MIT-licensed, in one repo,

00:07:20.397 --> 00:07:21.809
with documentation online.

00:07:22.197 --> 00:07:23.209
Edgepad is free.

00:07:23.647 --> 00:07:24.409
Find it on GitHub.
